{
  // The boy-scout rule for skills: leave a SKILL.md you touch cleaner than you found it.
  // Each list is what breaks a rule on the checked-out tree (the scripts in scripts/ print
  // it). A pull request fails if it changes a file that is on a list, so the fix comes with
  // the change. Nobody has to fix a file they didn't touch, and there is no baseline to keep.
  // https://github.com/ai-ecoverse/boy-scout
  "lists": [
    {
      "name": "skill-md-too-long",
      "command": "node scripts/check-skills.mjs --list too-long",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, bring the SKILL.md to 500 lines or fewer.",
        "Keep what an agent gets wrong without it. Move the rest to references/ and",
        "link it by a path that exists. See AGENTS.md, Skills."
      ]
    },
    {
      // What a SKILL.md says is in the context of every session that loads the skill. A
      // skill with an eval may have 5,000 tokens, which the Agent Skills specification
      // recommends as the most. A skill without one may have 1,000: nobody has shown yet
      // that what it says changes what an agent does.
      "name": "skill-md-over-token-limit",
      "command": "node scripts/check-skills.mjs --list over-token-limit",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, bring the SKILL.md under its limit: 5,000",
        "tokens for a skill with an eval, 1,000 for one without. Either give the skill",
        "an eval: skills/<skill>/evals/evals.json, or a scenario evals/<skill>-<what it",
        "tests>/ in its plugin with task.md and criteria.json (CONTRIBUTING.md, Evals).",
        "Or cut it: keep what an agent gets wrong without it and move the rest to",
        "references/. Run node scripts/check-skills.mjs --tokens <plugin dir> to see",
        "each skill's tokens, limit and eval."
      ]
    },
    {
      // What `tessl plugin lint` warns about, for plugins with a Tessl manifest. Needs the
      // tessl CLI. A warning about a skill is on its SKILL.md; any other is on the plugin's
      // .tessl-plugin/plugin.json.
      "name": "tessl-lint-warning",
      "command": "node scripts/tessl-lint-debt.mjs",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, clear what tessl plugin lint warns about for",
        "this file. Run node scripts/tessl-lint-debt.mjs --verbose to see the warning.",
        "For a SKILL.md over the token limit: keep what an agent gets wrong without it",
        "and move the rest to references/."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "skill-name-twice-in-plugin",
      "command": "node scripts/check-skills.mjs --list duplicate-in-plugin",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, give the skill a name that no other skill of",
        "its plugin has: the frontmatter name and its folder, and every place that",
        "names it (manifests, routing skills, links). Run node scripts/check-skills.mjs",
        "to see which skill it collides with."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "skill-name-in-two-plugins",
      "command": "node scripts/check-skills.mjs --list duplicate-across-plugins",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, give the skill a name that no other plugin",
        "has, for example with the product or runtime in it (#497). GitHub Copilot CLI",
        "exposes skills under their bare name, so two installed plugins with a",
        "same-named skill are ambiguous. Renaming one of the two clears both. Run",
        "node scripts/check-skills.mjs to see which skill it collides with."
      ]
    },
    {
      // A SKILL.md that no client finds. Clients read the folders directly under a
      // plugin's skills/ and don't look further (https://agent-plugins.org/specification,
      // Skills); Claude Code also reads what its manifest lists under "skills".
      "name": "orphaned-skill",
      "command": "node scripts/check-skills.mjs --list orphaned",
      "fix": [
        "Fix: in this same pull request, make the skill one a client finds, or stop",
        "calling it a skill. A plugin's skills are the folders directly under skills/;",
        "no client looks below them (#497). Either move it to skills/<name>/, with a",
        "name no other skill has. Or, if a parent skill loads it as a reference, rename",
        "the file so that it is no SKILL.md (for example references/<name>.md) and link",
        "it from the parent. Listing its folder under \"skills\" for the Claude Code",
        "target in plugin.json makes it found in Claude Code only. Run",
        "node scripts/check-skills.mjs to see where it lies."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
